## Why This Is Asked

Understanding data leakage and proper evaluation on small datasets is critical for reliable models. This question tests practical thinking, not theory alone, and guards against tempting but flawed splits that could invalidate results.

## Key Concepts

- Data leakage and temporal splits
- Baseline models and feature encoding
- Evaluation metrics and calibration
- Time-aware validation strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple logistic regression gradient step (conceptual)
function step(w, b, x, y, lr) {
  const z = 1 / (1 + Math.exp(-(dot(w, x) + b)));
  const error = y - z;
  // Update weights and bias
  for (let i = 0; i < w.length; i++) {
    w[i] += lr * error * x[i];
  }
  b += lr * error;
  return { w, b };
}
```

This example demonstrates the core gradient descent logic while keeping the implementation minimal and focused on the mathematical foundation.

## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to design scalable, tenant-aware ML pipelines with calibration, streaming features, drift handling, and safe rollout strategies across enterprise-scale tenants.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant feature stores and leakage prevention
- Shared base model + per-tenant calibrator
- Real-time features from streaming usage and billing
- Online retraining with drift detectors
- Offline + online evaluation and staged rollout

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo calibration hook
function calibrate(probs, tenantId, store){
  const params = store.getParams(tenantId)
  // adjust by temp scaler
  return Math.min(0.999, Math.max(0.001, probs * params.scale + params.bias))
}
```

